      "transcript_text": "Ok. Now let us also talk about another kind of a business which is going to be our discussion focus as far as our course is concerned. That kind of a business is called as a company or a corporation kind of a business. Now a company unlike a proprietorship or a partnership is a separate legal entity. A company can sue others and it can also be sued by others. Ok. Now the question is what are the owners of a corporation kind of a business called as? They are called as shareholders. You must be wondering how many owners or shareholders can a corporation have? Can a company have? The answer is it depends on whether your company is a private limited company or it is a public limited company. Yet another question you might have is is there a specific law to regulate a company kind of a business? The answer is yes. A company kind of a business is regulated under the Indian Companies Act 2030. Ok. Now let us talk about some of the features of a company kind of a business. In the case of a company or a corporation kind of a business, shareholders have limited liability. This is in contrast to unlimited liability that proprietors and partners have. What is the meaning of limited liability? The meaning of limited liability is that as the name implies liability of shareholders is limited to the amount of wealth they have contributed at the time of buying the shares of the firm. Which means that shareholders can lose no more than the wealth they have contributed at the time of buying their shares. Their personal wealth is not at stake even if the company owes some money to somebody else which the company is unable to repay. Also unlike a proprietorship or a partnership kind of a business, a company has perpetual life. Why? Even if managers quit or they are dismissed, the company continues to survive. Today shareholders can sell off their shares to new investors without disrupting the operations of the business. And that is also a reason as to why a corporation is also called as a going concern. Which means that it will keep on going on and on forever till the point it encounters an event such as bankruptcy or an acquisition. However, a company suffers from one important disadvantage relative to a partnership and proprietorship kind of a business. Can you think of that disadvantage? Of course there can be many disadvantages. Here the disadvantage that I am going to talk about it relates to a financial disadvantage. Okay. A company kind of a business is subject to separating contacts on business income. And this is in addition to personal tax that shareholders have to pay on their own. In other words, a company kind of a business suffers from something called as double taxation. First of all, a company has to pay taxes at the rate of prevailing corporate income tax rate to the government. And thereafter, whatever income a company decides to pay out to each shareholders, the dividends are going to be taxable in the hands of shareholders.",
